## Approved change plan (trusted, skill-controlled)

```yaml
{{ input.plan | tojson(indent=2) if input.plan is defined else '(missing)' }}
```

## Task

For every `change_plan.files[]` entry, check the file on disk:

1. `created` / `modified`: the file exists and implements `summary`.
2. `deleted`: the file is gone and nothing references it.
3. Changes outside the plan's files are findings (scope creep).

Skip anything in the lint list.

Each finding carries a fixed code and severity (rule-codes.md §5):
DSN-1-1 / 95 for a planned file missing or not implementing its summary,
DSN-1-2 / 90 for a deleted file still referenced, DSN-1-3 / 75 for a
change outside the plan. Rate `confidence` 90-100 when proven from the plan
and the cited file, 80-89 with one fact assumed, 70-79 when a deciding
file was not read; below 70, discard.

## Untrusted source: lint findings

```text
{% for f in input.lint_findings %}
- {{ f.file_line }} — {{ f.title }}
{% else %}
- (none)
{% endfor %}
```

## Output

```bash
LOOM={{ input.__loom.runtime }}
WD={{ input.__loom.workdir }}
$LOOM output init "$WD" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}'
$LOOM output add "$WD" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}' \
    --set 'findings[].title=<short>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].file_line=<skill-relative path>:<line>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].description=<what differs from the plan>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].fix=<concrete change>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].check_id=DSN-1-1' \
    --set 'findings[-1].severity=95' \
    --set 'findings[-1].confidence=<70-100>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].source={{ input.__task.id }}'
```

No findings: `--set-json 'findings=[]'`.
